            "path": "C:\\Users\\klimp\\OneDrive\\Documents\\Paradox Interactive\\Hearts of Iron IV\\mod\\chaos_redux\\paradox_wiki\\Data structures - Hearts of Iron 4 Wiki.md",
            "startLine": 1667,
            "endLine": 1682,
            "excerpt": "## Game variables <a id=\"Game_variables\"></a> Game variables are read-only variables that are used to read certain aspects of the game, such as the current political power that the player has. These cannot be modified using any variable-modifying argument, but they can serve as the value within them",
            "authority": "Offline Paradox Wiki snapshot",
            "sectionStartLine": 1458,
            "sectionEndLine": 1778,
            "startColumn": 1,
            "text": "State-scoped game variables:\n\n| Variable | Target | Description/Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| id | None. | The internal ID of the state. While regular `set_variable = { my_state_pointer = 123 }` would still work as a pointer to the state, this can remove ambiguity within the code whether the number is used as a state ID or the number that refers to the state with the state ID of 123. **Not the same value as the state ID** defined with `id=123` in the file, typically returns some negative number instead. For fetching the state ID, a [meta effect](<Effects - Hearts of Iron 4 Wiki.md>) using [the GetID namespace](<Localisation - Hearts of Iron 4 Wiki.md>) can be used. |\n| building_level | Building such as `@nuclear_reactor`. | The level of a building with the target type. |\n| arms_factory_level | None. | Military factory level in the state |\n| industrial_complex_level | None. | civilian factory level in the state |\n| infrastructure_level | None. | infrastructure level in the state |\n| damaged_building_level | Building such as `@industrial_complex`. | Damaged building level of a building with target type. |\n| non_damaged_building_level | Building such as `@arms_factory`. | Non-damaged building level of a building with target type. |\n| modifier | Modifier's name, such as `@political_power_gain`. | The total value of the current [modifier](<Modifiers - Hearts of Iron 4 Wiki.md>) as the country has in total. Targeted modifiers have separate definitions. |\n| controller | None. | Controller of the state. |\n| owner | None. | Owner of the state. |\n| distance_to | State. | Distance between the current state and the target state. |\n| resource | Resource type such as `@chromium` | Amount of the resource produced within state. |",
            "nextLine": 1683,
            "nextColumn": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
